  "executive_briefing": "As of late August 2026, the digital asset ecosystem is anchored by imminent regulatory milestones and structural technical evolutions. The upcoming U.S. Senate cloture vote on September 15 for the Digital Asset Market Clarity Act (H.R. 3633) represents the definitive regulatory catalyst for U.S. market structure. Concurrently, institutional Bitcoin flows via ETFs and corporate treasuries remain in a consolidation phase following the first net annual outflows recorded in H1 2026. Architecturally, institutional smart contract preferences are bifurcating: while Ethereum (EVM) retains unmatched ecosystem liquidity, Bitcoin-native deterministic execution models like Clarity are surging as risk-averse enterprises demand decidable, non-Turing-complete smart contracts to eliminate reentrancy risks. Parallelly, cross-chain DeFi is systematically abandoning vulnerable wrapped-token bridges in favor of native, non-custodial direct swap liquidity routing between Bitcoin and Ethereum.",
